  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "CORE MECHANICS",
    "heading": "ARMOR",
    "lineStart": 3905,
    "lineEnd": 4015,
    "pdfPageStart": 72,
    "pdfPageEnd": 74
  },
  "rulesText": "Every armor has a name, base damage thresholds, and a base Armor Score. Some armor also has a feature.\n\n- An armor’s base armor score indicates how many Armor Slots it provides its wearer before additional bonuses are added to calculate their total Armor Score. A PC’s Armor Score can’t exceed 12.\n- An armor’s base thresholds determine its wearer’s Major and Severe damage thresholds before adding bonuses to calculate their final damage thresholds. When recording your character’s damage thresholds in the “Damage & Health” section of your character sheet, you always add your character’s level to those values.\n- An armor’s feature is a special rule that stays in effect while the armor is equipped.\n\nWhile unarmored, your character’s base Armor Score is 0, their Major threshold is equal to their level, and their Severe threshold is equal to twice their level.\n\n##### REDUCING INCOMING DAMAGE\n\nWhen you take damage, you can mark one Armor Slot to reduce the severity of the damage by one threshold (Severe to Major, Major to Minor, Minor to nothing). If your character has an Armor Score of 0, you can’t mark Armor Slots. If an effect temporarily increases your Armor Score, it increases your available Armor Slots by the same amount; when the effect ends, so does the availability of these Armor Slots.\n\n#### ARMOR TABLES\n\n##### TIER 1 (LEVEL 1)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Mage Robes | 4 / 10 | 2 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Gambeson Armor | 5 / 11 | 3 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Brigandine Armor | 6 / 12 | 3 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Leather Armor | 6 / 13 | 3 | — |\n| Scale Mail Armor | 7 / 14 | 3 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Chainmail Armor | 7 / 15 | 4 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Banded Armor | 8 / 16 | 4 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Full Plate Armor | 8 / 17 | 4 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n\n##### TIER 2 (LEVELS 2–4)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Improved Mage Robes | 6 / 15 | 3 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Improved Gambeson Armor | 7 / 16 | 4 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Improved Brigandine Armor | 9 / 19 | 4 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Improved Leather Armor | 9 / 20 | 4 | — |\n| Improved Scale Mail Armor | 11 / 23 | 4 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Improved Chainmail Armor | 11 / 24 | 5 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Improved Banded Armor | 13 / 27 | 5 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Improved Full Plate Armor | 13 / 28 | 5 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n| Enchanter’s Robes | 9 / 20 | 4 | Mnemonic: Once per scene, you can recall a domain card from your vault without paying its Recall Cost. |\n| Hawkguard’s Mantle | 9 / 20 | 4 | Gliding: You can glide up to Far range and are immune to damage from falling. |\n| Spidersilk Tunic | 9 / 20 | 4 | Wall-Crawling: +1 Evasion; you can walk on walls as easily as on the ground. |\n\n| | | | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Stormthread Habit | 9 / 20 | 4 | Absorbing: Once per scene when you take magic damage, you can clear an Armor Slot. |\n| Elundrian Chain Armor | 9 / 21 | 4 | Warded: You reduce incoming magic damage by your Armor Score before applying it to your damage thresholds. |\n| Harrowbone Armor | 9 / 21 | 4 | Resilient: Before you mark your last Armor Slot, roll a d6. On a result of 6, reduce the severity by one threshold without marking an Armor Slot. |\n| Irontree Breastplate Armor | 9 / 20 | 4 | Reinforced: When you mark your last Armor Slot, increase your damage thresholds by +2 until you clear at least 1 Armor Slot. |\n| Runetan Floating Armor | 9 / 20 | 4 | Shifting: When you are targeted for an attack, you can mark an Armor Slot to give the attack roll against you disadvantage. |\n| Tyris Soft Armor | 8 / 18 | 5 | Quiet: You gain a +2 bonus to rolls you make to move silently. |\n| Wyrdwood Splint Armor | 10 / 21 | 5 | Quick-Striding: You can’t be Restrained and can move up to Far range as part of an action roll. |\n| Rosewild Armor | 11 / 23 | 5 | Hopeful: When you would spend a Hope, you can mark an Armor Slot instead. |\n| Trollhide Cuirass | 11 / 23 | 5 | Self-Healing: When you take a rest, clear an Armor Slot. |\n| Gilded Sunplate | 12 / 26 | 5 | Resplendent: Once per scene when you spend Hope, you can clear an Armor Slot. |\n\n##### TIER 3 (LEVELS 5–7)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Advanced Mage Robes | 8 / 22 | 4 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Advanced Gambeson Armor | 9 / 23 | 5 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Advanced Brigandine Armor | 11 / 26 | 5 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Advanced Leather Armor | 11 / 27 | 5 | — |\n| Advanced Scale Mail Armor | 13 / 30 | 5 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Advanced Chainmail Armor | 13 / 31 | 6 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Advanced Banded Armor | 15 / 34 | 6 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Advanced Full Plate Armor | 15 / 35 | 6 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n| Granminster’s Finery | 11 / 27 | 2 | Magnificent: Gain a bonus to your Armor Score equal to your Presence. |\n| Spiked Plate Armor | 10 / 25 | 5 | Sharp: On a successful attack against a target within Melee range, add a d4 to the damage roll. |\n| Astral Raiment | 11 / 27 | 5 | Stellar: Mark a Stress to gain advantage on a Spellcast roll. |\n| Bellamoi Fine Armor | 11 / 27 | 5 | Gilded: +1 to Presence |\n| Cloverweave Cloak | 11 / 27 | 5 | Fortune-Favored: Once per scene, you can change a failure with Hope into a success with Fear. |\n| Dragonscale Armor | 11 / 27 | 5 | Impenetrable: Once per short rest, when you would mark your last Hit Point, you can instead mark a Stress. |\n| Skywarden’s Lamellar | 11 / 27 | 5 | Vigilant: +2 to Evasion |\n| Bloodstone Plate Armor | 13 / 35 | 6 | Bloodthirsty: When you critically succeed on a weapon attack within Melee range, clear a Hit Point. |\n| Deep-Forged Coral Armor | 13 / 35 | 6 | Aquatic: You can breathe underwater and gain advantage on Agility Rolls while submerged. |\n| Bladefare Armor | 16 / 39 | 6 | Physical: You can’t mark an Armor Slot to reduce magic damage. |\n| Monett’s Cloak | 16 / 39 | 6 | Magic: You can’t mark an Armor Slot to reduce physical damage. |\n| Runes of Fortification | 17 / 43 | 6 | Painful: Each time you mark an Armor Slot, you must mark a Stress. |\n\n##### TIER 4 (LEVELS 8–10)\n\n| Name | Base Thresholds | Base Score | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Legendary Mage Robes | 10 / 31 | 5 | Enchanted: Gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your Spellcast trait. |\n| Legendary Gambeson Armor | 11 / 32 | 6 | Flexible: +1 to Evasion |\n| Legendary Brigandine Armor | 13 / 35 | 6 | Lined: Mark a Stress to negate Minor damage. |\n| Legendary Leather Armor | 13 / 36 | 6 | — |\n| Legendary Scale Mail Armor | 15 / 39 | 6 | Cumbersome: −1 to Finesse |\n| Legendary Chainmail Armor | 15 / 40 | 7 | Heavy: −1 to Evasion |\n| Legendary Banded Armor | 17 / 43 | 7 | Bulky: −1 to Evasion; when you take Severe damage, you must mark a Stress. |\n| Legendary Full Plate Armor | 17 / 44 | 7 | Very Heavy: −2 to Evasion; −1 to Agility |\n| Full Fortified Armor | 15 / 40 | 4 | Fortified: When you mark an Armor Slot, you reduce the severity of an attack by two thresholds instead of one. |\n| Channeling Armor | 13 / 36 | 5 | Channeling: +1 to Spellcast Rolls |\n| Darkweave Shroud | 13 / 36 | 5 | Ghostwalker: Once per rest, mark a Stress to move up to Close range through solid objects. |\n| Emberwoven Armor | 13 / 36 | 6 | Burning: When an adversary attacks you within Melee range, they mark a Stress. |\n| Godbound Laminar | 13 / 36 | 6 | Divine: When you mark an Armor Slot, gain a Hope. |\n| Veritas Opal Armor | 13 / 36 | 6 | Truthseeking: This armor glows when another creature within Close range tells a lie. |\n| Circle-Forged Dreadplate | 14 / 38 | 6 | Accursed: When you mark any number of Hit Points from an attack, roll a d4. On a result of 4, the attacker must mark an equal number of Stress. |\n| Rune-Forged Exosuit | 12 / 39 | 7 | Attuned: The maximum number of domain cards in your loadout is reduced by one, but you gain a bonus to your damage thresholds equal to your tier. |\n| Dunamis Silkchain | 13 / 36 | 7 | Timeslowing: Mark an Armor Slot to roll a d4 and add its result as a bonus to your Evasion against an incoming attack. |\n| Hallowed Heroplate | 13 / 35 | 7 | Blessed: Once per long rest, you can spend any number of Hope before you make the Risk It All death move. You gain a bonus to the result of your Hope Die equal to the number of Hope spent. |\n| Resonant Harness | 15 / 40 | 7 | Vitreous: When you would take Severe or greater damage, you can mark 2 Armor Slots to negate that damage. If you do, you gain a −5 penalty to your damage thresholds until you choose to repair your armor as a downtime move. |\n| Savior Chainmail | 18 / 48 | 8 | Difficult: −1 to all character traits and Evasion |",
  "htmlPage": {
    "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/daggerheart-system-json/records/rules/armor/"
  },
